    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi prof, i am having a bit of trouble with phonetics. can u explain the difference between voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives? like why is /z/ different from /s/ when they are made in the same place?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The key difference between $/z/$ and $/s/$ lies in vocal cord vibration; $/s/$ is an unvoiced sound, meaning your vocal cords do not vibrate when you produce it. In contrast, $/z/$ is a voiced sound, requiring the vocal cords to vibrate simultaneously while forcing air through the same alveolar constriction. This vibration is what gives $/z/$ its distinct humming quality compared to the purely breathy sound of $/s/$.",
